  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on variance, which quantifies outcome dispersion. The individual, however, focuses on minimizing the maximum possible loss (i.e., the worst outcome), which aligns with a minimax or loss-aversion heuristic, not variance minimization. While both approaches may lead to choosing Lottery B in this case, the justification is based on the magnitude of the worst outcome, not on the spread of outcomes. There is no mention or implication of considering how much the outcomes vary around the mean. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not match the variance-based decision rule, even though the final choice may coincide.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
